      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "On a server node, one k3s process runs the whole control plane: the API server, scheduler, controller manager and datastore."
        },
        {
          "text": "It also runs the node pieces, the kubelet, containerd and Flannel, so the server can run your pods too."
        },
        {
          "text": "Agent nodes run a smaller k3s process with just the node pieces, and join the cluster by pointing at the server."
        },
        {
          "text": "For this series, picture one server and two agents, on machines in your own rack, not in a cloud."
        },
        {
          "text": "One server is fine for learning; for high availability you'd run three servers that share an embedded etcd.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "install",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "admin@k3s-server-1",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "curl -sfL https://get.k3s.io | sh -",
          "output": [
            "[INFO]  Finding release for channel stable",
            "[INFO]  Using v1.33.5+k3s1 as release",
            "[INFO]  Installing k3s to /usr/local/bin/k3s",
            "[INFO]  systemd: Enabling k3s unit",
            "[INFO]  systemd: Starting k3s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "sudo cat /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/node-token",
          "output": [
            "K10f3c9a1e7b2::server:8d41c07a6be95f2e"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Installing a server takes one command."
        },
        {
          "text": "The install script downloads the binary and starts k3s as a system service."
        },
        {
          "text": "The server also writes a join token, a shared secret that agents need before they're allowed in."
        },
        {
          "text": "Treat it like a password, because anyone holding it can add a node to your cluster.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "join",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "admin@k3s-agent-1",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "export K3S_URL=https://k3s-server-1:6443",
          "output": []
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "export K3S_TOKEN=K10f3c9a1e7b2::server:8d41c07a6be95f2e",
          "output": []
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "curl -sfL https://get.k3s.io | sh -",
          "output": [
            "[INFO]  Using v1.33.5+k3s1 as release",
            "[INFO]  Installing k3s to /usr/local/bin/k3s",
            "[INFO]  systemd: Enabling k3s-agent unit",
            "[INFO]  systemd: Starting k3s-agent"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "On each agent, set the server's address, on port 6443, where the API server listens."
        },
        {
          "text": "Then set the token you just copied."
        },
        {
          "text": "Run the same installer, and because those two settings are present, it installs an agent instead.",
          "senses": {
            "present": "adjective"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nodes",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "ssh k3s-server-1 sudo cat /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml > ~/.kube/config",
          "output": []
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "sed -i 's/127.0.0.1/k3s-server-1/' ~/.kube/config",
          "output": []
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "kubectl get nodes",
          "output": [
            "NAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE   VERSION",
            "k3s-server-1   Ready    control-plane,master   12d   v1.33.5+k3s1",
            "k3s-agent-1    Ready    <none>                 12d   v1.33.5+k3s1",
            "k3s-agent-2    Ready    <none>                 12d   v1.33.5+k3s1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Back on your laptop, copy the kubeconfig file that k3s wrote on the server."
        },
        {
          "text": "It points at the server's own loopback address, so swap in the server's name."
        },
        {
          "text": "Now kubectl can talk to the API server, and the first thing to check is the nodes."
        },
        {
          "text": "Three nodes, all Ready: the server has the control plane role, and the agents have none.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
