      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "k3s also ships the add-ons a cluster needs on day one, so it works out of the box."
        },
        {
          "text": "Flannel gives every pod its own IP address, and lets pods on different nodes reach each other."
        },
        {
          "text": "CoreDNS lets pods find services by name, so the API can ask for Postgres instead of an IP address."
        },
        {
          "text": "Traefik is the ingress controller: it takes HTTP traffic from outside and routes it to the right service."
        },
        {
          "text": "ServiceLB gives load balancer services an address on your own nodes, since on-prem there's no cloud to hand one out."
        },
        {
          "text": "And local-path storage carves volumes out of a node's disk, which is where our database will keep its data."
        },
        {
          "text": "Each one gets a closer look later; for now, just know they're there.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kube-system",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl get pods -n kube-system",
          "output": [
            "NAME                                      READY   STATUS      RESTARTS   AGE",
            "coredns-697968c856-7wqxk                  1/1     Running     0          12d",
            "helm-install-traefik-crd-6kx8q            0/1     Completed   0          12d",
            "helm-install-traefik-tq2fm                0/1     Completed   1          12d",
            "local-path-provisioner-774c6665dc-m4tzl   1/1     Running     0          12d",
            "metrics-server-6f4c6675d5-9pjbh           1/1     Running     0          12d",
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-6hx2r              2/2     Running     0          12d",
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-qw8lm              2/2     Running     0          12d",
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-zk5vn              2/2     Running     0          12d",
            "traefik-c98fdf6fb-kq7xn                   1/1     Running     0          12d"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Most of those add-ons run as ordinary pods, in a namespace called kube-system."
        },
        {
          "text": "The two helm install pods are one-off jobs that set up Traefik, so Completed is exactly what you want to see."
        },
        {
          "text": "There's one svclb pod per node: that's ServiceLB, holding Traefik's ports open on every machine."
        },
        {
          "text": "Notice what's missing: no API server, no scheduler and no Flannel, because those live inside the k3s process itself.",
          "senses": {
            "live": "verb"
          },
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
